  title: Jainism
  text: Jainism teaches that the soul can be freed through right faith, right knowledge and right conduct. Jains revere twenty-four tirthankaras, or ford-makers; the first was Rishabhanatha, the twenty-third Parshvanatha and the twenty-fourth Mahavira.
